title: Paradigm Docs Platform — First Live Run + SPA Catch-All Fix
summary: First live test of `paradigm docs serve` revealed the docs section hanging on "Loading..." — traced to Express 5's SPA catch-all wildcard swallowing `/api/*` requests without calling `next()`. One-line fix. The manifest API now serves 1,179 symbols across 8 groups in ~25ms. The Platform UI docs tab works but needs polish passes on sidebar UX, page layouts, and the custom pages section (currently showing raw docs/ files instead of the handwritten guides).
symbols_touched:
  - '#DocsSection'
  - '#DocsRouter'
  - '#PlatformServer'
files_modified:
  - packages/paradigm/src/platform-server/index.ts
decisions:
  - id: D-spa-catchall-next
    decision: Add next() call to Express 5 SPA catch-all when path starts with /api
    rationale: Without next(), any API route mounted after the catch-all (via dynamic import in startPlatformServer) would hang forever. This was a latent bug affecting docs, symphony, and sentinel routes.
errors_encountered:
  - description: paradigm docs serve showed 'Loading...' forever — /api/docs/manifest hung with no response
    resolution: SPA catch-all in Express 5 matched /api/* but didn't call next() — added else { next(); } branch
    time_to_fix: 15 minutes
learnings:
  - Express 5 wildcard routes ({*path}) match everything including /api/* — always call next() for paths you don't handle, or the request hangs silently
  - The docs manifest generates in ~25ms for 1,179 symbols — no performance concern even for large projects
  - Dynamic route mounting after the SPA fallback requires the fallback to be a proper middleware (call next), not a terminal handler
